      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grizzly_Flats%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Prospectors named the town after a grizzly bear they saw in 1850.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grizzly_Flats%2C_California",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1852 the settlement covered about a mile by three‑quarters of a mile and housed two bars, stores, and boarding houses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grizzly_Flats%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A post office opened in 1854, a stagecoach route to Diamond Springs followed in 1855, and a Wells Fargo office arrived in 1857.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grizzly_Flats%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Caldor Fire in August 2021 destroyed roughly 500 buildings, including the historic 1850s post office and Walt Tyler Elementary School.",
